can be very prolific. A writer may find himself writing easily and comfortably, and his creativity will express itself well. Love relationships will also be harmonious.
Relationships with friends, hopes, wishes, goals, and aspirations are linked to the eleventh-house cusp. If this progressed cusp makes good aspects, friends will be plentiful and loyal. If it makes harsh aspects, it will be difficult to fulfill goals and aspirations and there will be disappointment with friends.
When the progressed eleventh-house cusp conjuncted my Ascendant, I was asked to be on the board of the American Federation of Astrologers (AFA). I jokingly tell my students that when the progressed eleventh-house cusp makes an easy aspect to Jupiter, "Be careful of what you wish for, as you will create it." You will also attract spiritual people, foreigners, and Sagittarians. When it makes a harmonious aspect to Venus, you will draw in a lot of creative, loving friends, perhaps a Taurus or a Libra.
When it makes an aspect to Uranus, your friends will be different or unusual in some way, such as an Aquarian. An aspect to Neptune brings spiritual, artistic companions such as a Pisces, and aspects to Pluto bring powerful people such as a Scorpio. It may be a person with either that Sun sign or rising sign who enters your life.
The Axis of Service and Sacrifice
The cusps of the sixth and twelfth houses have to do with productivity, working conditions and environment, health, service, sacrifice, and karma. The twelfth house is often referred to as the house of self-undoing, but it need not be so. However, service to odiers is demanded when there is a twelfth-house emphasis.
When the progressed sixth-house cusp makes good aspects to a planet, there is good interaction with coworkers. There is a positive work environment. You could attract good employees. Management and labor get along well. You tend to be extremely productive and have a lot of physical energy and vitality. Under harsh aspects, there could be difficulty at work and health problems. A
square to Mars may indicate surgery, a square to Saturn suggests a chronic illness, and a square to Jupiter can reflect dissipation and overindulgence.

Progressions involving the twelfth-house cusp indicate confinement, self-sacrifice, and the workings of the subconscious. I had a client who was confined to a Mexican jail for possession of marijuana when his progressed twelfth-house cusp squared natal and progressed Saturn. He was incarcerated for four years. Again, I must state that there were other reinforcing aspects at work.
The most positive twelfth-house aspects depict a person working well alone, enjoying his or her own company, and doing solitary projects. This is also a great time to do research. Interests such as yoga and meditation are rewarding. When the progressed twelfth-house cusp squares a planet, however, you could be your own worst enemy A square to Mars could indicate self-destructive behavior.
Some squares from the progressed twelfth-house cusp may also suggest periods of deep withdrawal and isolation. Good aspects can result in incredible psychological breakthroughs. You could become involved in a behind-the-scenes job, hospice work, or community service. It is a time when you can make positive contributions to the world.
Since so few astrologers use the progressed house cusps, there is little written data on how this system operates. I suggest that astrologers observe the cusps and note the results. This is particularly true of the succedent and cadent houses rather than the angular houses. Some research has been done on angular houses. Another value I find in this system is in chart rectification. If the anticipated activity is not present, I question the client about the source of the birth time.
