is making no adverse aspects. Other planets can have some affliction to add spice or energy to the event, but the Moon should be perfect. No squares and preferably no oppositions, although they can be tolerated.
Sun Transits
The Sun rules our ego and will. Sun transits are often triggers for heavy transits and progressions. On a day when the transiting Sun aspects our Venus or Jupiter, we can feel positive, optimistic, and attractive. When the transiting Sun aspects Mars, we will experience more energy. When the Sun transits Saturn, we could feel more serious and authoritative. An aspect to Uranus is more magnetic, to Neptune more creative, and to Pluto more powerful.
Mercury Transits
Mercury is the planet of communication. For a writer or speaker, transits from Mercury will be helpful. You can pinpoint days when you will be more prolific as a writer or days when you will receive important

news or letters. You can concentrate well under any Mercury/Saturn transit. Mercury/Jupiter tends to exaggerate, and Mercury/Uranus gets flashes of insight. Mercury/Neptune can be inspired writing, and Mercury/Pluto or Mercury/Mars can be outbursts of temper.
Venus Transits
Venus is the planet of love and beauty. Under good transits from Venus, we feel loved, emotionally secure, and attractive. These are the days when our hair turns out beautifully, our makeup goes on well, we find beautiful things when we shop, and socializing is enjoyable.
Venus transiting Mars is good for sexual compatibility, and Venus transiting Jupiter can be extravagant. Venus transiting Saturn can define love, and Venus with Uranus can bring a sudden love experience or unusual events. If you begin a love relationship with Venus to Uranus, or Uranus to Venus, it can be over as quickly
