as it started. Venus to Neptune can love unconditionally and is exceptionally creative. When Venus connects to Pluto, you have a deep need to be loved and can be compulsive and obsessive about love or a loved one.
Mars Transits
Mars rules our energy. It is often referred to as the timekeeper of the zodiac. Mars is the planet we can use to rectify a chart. When Mars crosses the Ascendant, its energy is felt and there is usually an event. I remember telling my husband that I didn't feel his time of birth was exactly correct, so I changed his Ascendant degree. I said, "If I am right, today when Mars crosses your Ascendant you may get a headache." He said, "I never get headaches." I said, "Well, if I am right, something will happen." Later that day, he broke off a tooth eating popcorn so I knew I had the right Ascendant. I was never sure of my exact birth time either. My baby book said one thing and my birth certificate another. So I watched Mars in Capricorn very closely. One day I got up very quickly from where I was sitting and bumped my knee on the coffee table. I got a big, huge bruise. I was very excited because I knew that the degree Mars was at that day was the correct degree of my Ascendant, because Capricorn rules the knees and Mars can be a minor injury.
Jupiter Transits
The planet Jupiter is known as the "great benefic." It is the transit for which we all wait. It is known as the expander, the planet of luck, opportunity, and good fortune. The planet Jupiter is expansive,

stimulating, buoyant, and optimistic. However, I have found many times that it brings flash-in-the-pan success, rather than something of lasting value. I find that I benefit more from a nice Saturn trine than I ever do from a Jupiter trine. This is where the fall and detriment of the planets are important. This attitude reflects the experience in my chart. I have Jupiter in Virgo. It is not well placed in this sign. Somebody with Jupiter in Sagittarius will
have a much more significant gain with a Jupiter transit than I will. I also have Saturn in Aquarius. It is well placed here, and therefore my benefits under transiting Saturn tend to be positive.
One thing I tell my students when they are viewing Jupiter transits through the chart is that if things are positive in the natal chart and positive with progressions and other transits, Jupiter can make them even better. But if your chart is difficult, and you have negative, heavy transits and negative progressions, Jupiter can make things worse. What you have to remember is that Jupiter will expand and enhance whatever is going on. I have seen people who had great Jupiter transits, but things just got worse because of the rest of the influences in operation.
While a Jupiter transit over a planet can be very brief, there is much more benefit when Jupiter transits over a stellium of planets. Also, I find Jupiter to be quite beneficial to any house through which it is transiting because of the duration of time spent there.
