When Jupiter transits the second house, enters the sign Taurus, or aspects Venus, money-making opportunities seem to increase, but so does the tendency to be overly optimistic about money and to spend too much. Jupiter is the planet of extravagance as well as abundance.
Personal values can become more spiritual, and we are inclined to be more generous. Whenever Jupiter and Venus come together, it is a time of increased luck. It's a good time to buy a lottery ticket.
