i^ymations happen every month. Traditionally, the term lunation refers to the New Moon and Full Moon. The New Moon is the beginning of the lunar month. It starts when the Sun and Moon are conjunct in the same sign at the same degree and minute. The Moon waxes, or grows toward full, in the heavens until it creates an opposition with the Sun, at which time we have a Full Moon. Astrologically these two phases of the Moon are significant because the two houses in your chart where they fall are the areas of your life that will be energized and emphasized for that month.
The way I describe the lunations and eclipses to my students is that the New Moon and Solar Eclipse are both a time of beginnings, initiation, renewed energy, and vitality, a time of excitement and stimulation. The Full Moon and Lunar Eclipse are both a time of fruition, a time when issues, problems, or projects are finalized or resolved, many times

delivering what the New Moon 202 / Lunations and Eclipses
promised. Both lunations and eclipses offer opportunities to prioritize, focus, and put energy into those areas of your life that are accented by the lunation or eclipse. You are able to see and evaluate exactly what is important and what you need to do or change in your life.
I also tell my students that I can tell a lot about the coming year for a client just by looking at the eclipses and lunations. The lunations and eclipses are one of the most important predictive tools in astrology. To get a handle on what is happening in someone's life, look at where the eclipses fall for that year, and then follow the events with the New Moons and Full Moons. There is a pattern that forms.
I tell my students to buy a copy of the yearly Rosecrucian ephemeris. At the top of the page, next to the New Moon and Full Moon, write where each lunation and eclipse falls in the chart and what aspects they make, and then take notes of what happens. Using this method, you will have a journal to monitor what happens during the year, and you will grow to really understand how the eclipses and lunations work in your life. I have found this to be an excellent teaching tool.
You start the predictive process with the eclipses, and then you look at each of the lunations that follow Observe the sequence of aspects the lunations make to each other in the chart. The aspect sequence starts with the semisextile and then goes to the sextile. Next is the square, then the trine, then the quincunx or incon-junct, and finally the opposition.
There will be a correlation between these aspects to the events that happen in the person's life throughout the year.
For instance, if you start a relationship under a New Moon or Solar Eclipse in Leo, then the next month the New Moon in will be Virgo and will be in semisextile aspect to the initial lunation. This may be when you start dating and are getting to know one another. The second month the New Moon in Libra will be in sex-tile aspect to the initial lunation. The relationship may now look like it has promise and there is opportunity around it. You start to
