The eclipses, which are also lunations, have an added emphasis and a
much more intense focus. The New Moon Eclipse is called a Solar Eclipse. The Moon comes between the Earth and the Sun so that the sunlight is blocked either partially or fully. The Full Moon Eclipse is called a Lunar Eclipse. This happens when the Earth is between the Moon and the Sun, blocking the light of the Moon. There has always been a lot of hype about the dire consequences of eclipses. Often, I find that new students are overly concerned about them. When they see that an eclipse is falling on a planet in their chart, they fear something terrible will happen. This is not necessarily true. The eclipses and lunations work in harmony with the transits and progressions. Because of the beauty and the magnificent order of the universe, what the eclipses and lunations stimulate is pretty much what is already promised with the transits, progressions, and natal potential.
