Length of the Effect of an Eclipse
There are several theories as to the length of the effect of an eclipse.
One theory says that an eclipse will last until the next eclipse of the same type, with a waning effect until that time. For instance, if there is a Solar Eclipse in January, that eclipse will be in effect until the next Solar Eclipse in June or July.
Another theory is that the length and strength of the eclipse are dependent on the length of the duration of the eclipse in the heavens. With an eclipse that lasts a long time, this is probably the one whose effect will last for three years. Yet another theory is that the total eclipse of the Sun (Solar Eclipse) is the strongest. The partial Solar Eclipses are next in strength, with the Lunar
Eclipses (no matter what type) the weakest. These are the theories. I agree with all of them and none of them. There is some truth to them all.
Another theory is that the people most affected by eclipses are people with a prominent Moon or Sun. So someone with prominent Cancer in the natal chart would be more affected by the Lunar Eclipse, and someone with prominent Leo would be more affected by the Solar Eclipse. Also, women would be more effected by the Lunar Eclipse, and

men more by the Solar Eclipse. Tm not sure this is true. I feel them all.
