Glossary
Apparent Retrograde Motion —This term refers to the slowing down of planets that makes them appear as if they are going backward.
Applying Aspect —This term refers to a planet that is moving towards an exact aspect with a slower-moving planet. An applying aspect can also be made as a planet applies towards a fixed point, such as the Midheaven or Ascendant.
Ascendant —The sign of the zodiac that is rising in the east at the moment of birth. Also referred to as the sign on the first house.
Aspect —The relationship between two planets, or the relationship between a planet and the Ascendant or Midheaven. It is the angular distance between these two points.
Birth Chart —The birth chart is also referred to as the horoscope. The birth chart is a circle divided into twelve parts, or houses, each of which describes a different area of life or experience.
